description:
benchbox-site drafts/PUBLISHING.md still describes the single-repo flow. Examples:
- line 7: "Blog content is developed under `_blog/` in the single `BenchBox-dev/BenchBox` repository";
- line 9: posts go live "when the change is replayed into that repository", a replay process that ended when site #44 removed the fidelity check;
- lines 57 and 63: `uv run python scripts/blog_content_validation.py`, a script that exists in neither repo (and Python is banned from the site, ADR D9);
- lines 112-150 and 167-175: copy to `docs/blog/` and edit the `docs/blog/index.md` toctree, which are core Sphinx paths deleted in #3096.

An author following it today cannot publish a post. Rewrite it for drafts/ to blog/ inside the site repo, with the site's own validation commands.
